# Test: a live edit of service { tftp-server } reaches the TFTP server.
# Initial config: tftp-server enabled with root-directory /srv/ze-tftp-a.
# After SIGHUP:   root-directory is /srv/ze-tftp-b, nothing else changes.
# Expected: tftpserver installs the reloaded config at apply and logs it with
#           the new root directory.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-plugin-reload-applies-or-refuses row 25, AC-1: tftpserver's
#            verify/apply pair rebinds its listeners for the reloaded config
#            (tftpServer.install).
# PREVENTS: the acked-and-dropped reload. With OnConfigure alone, the SDK
#           answers config-apply OK and calls nothing, so the commit succeeded
#           while the server kept serving the boot root-directory.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: the "/srv/ze-tftp-b" line is written only by install, which
# only the apply handler calls on a reload: without the handler the second
# expectation fails. That an edit elsewhere under service rebinds nothing is
# proven in Go by TestConfigTxUnchangedSubtreeIsNoop
# (tftpserver/config_tx_test.go). The listener names a device that does not
# exist, so on Linux the bind fails and is logged; the reload asserts the
# install, not the socket.

# skip-os linux: a reload binds every listen-interface or fails (R-13), and an
# unprivileged Linux host cannot bind port 69, so there the reload is refused.
# Darwin ignores the interface name and binds port 69 on every address, which
# an unprivileged user may. The strict bind and the cut transfer are proven in
# Go by TestConfigTxUnbindableInterfaceFailsApply and
# TestConfigTxReloadCutsTransferInFlight (tftpserver/config_tx_test.go).

option=skip-os:value=linux
option=env:var=ze.log.tftpserver:value=info

stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
service {
	tftp-server {
		enabled true
		listen-interface lo
		root-directory /srv/ze-tftp-a
		max-transfers 10
	}
}
EOF_CONF

tmpfs=config2.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF2
service {
	tftp-server {
		enabled true
		listen-interface lo
		root-directory /srv/ze-tftp-b
		max-transfers 10
	}
}
EOF_CONF2

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le test fixture reload/tx-protocol-sighup-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=20s
await=stderr:contains=sighup reload complete:then=stop
expect=stderr:pattern=tftpserver: config applied.*root-directory=/srv/ze-tftp-a
expect=stderr:pattern=tftpserver: config applied.*root-directory=/srv/ze-tftp-b
reject=stderr:contains=reload error
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
